From 0dab9830aee0dfb0c993c6eada14478dc97b6d7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:51:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 81/97] demux: ts: treat a title or seekpoint change as the
 seek it is

DEMUX_SET_TITLE and DEMUX_SET_SEEKPOINT handed the query straight to the
stream and did nothing else, while every other seek path in the module calls
ReadyQueuesPostSeek() first. A chapter jump therefore left behind the
continuity counters, the last dts and pcr of each program, the packets queued
for a pcr that will never come, and half-read sections - so the demuxer
reported the jump it was asked for as a break on every pid, and the first
block after it was never marked as one.

Reachable wherever the access offers seekpoints on a transport stream, which
for this module means a VDR recording: vdr.c turns STREAM_SET_SEEKPOINT into
a byte seek within the same recording.

Measured on a synthetic 48 s VDR recording, jumping to the second and third
cut marks: five "discontinuity received" warnings before, including one on
the audio pid for each jump, none after. The same two positions reached with
DEMUX_SET_TIME produced none either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
index a6041a366b..fc7b68289e 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
@@ -910,6 +910,7 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
     int64_t i64;
     int64_t *pi64;
     int i_int;
+    int i_ret;
     const ts_pmt_t *p_pmt = NULL;
     const ts_pat_t *p_pat = GetPID(p_sys, 0)->u.p_pat;
 
@@ -1140,11 +1141,18 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
     }
 
     case DEMUX_SET_TITLE:
-        return vlc_stream_vaControl( p_sys->stream, STREAM_SET_TITLE, args );
-
     case DEMUX_SET_SEEKPOINT:
-        return vlc_stream_vaControl( p_sys->stream, STREAM_SET_SEEKPOINT,
-                                     args );
+        /* The stream repositions itself, which is as much a seek as
+         * DEMUX_SET_TIME is, so leave behind what a seek leaves behind:
+         * continuity counters forgotten, queued packets dropped and the
+         * elementary streams told their data is not continuous. */
+        i_ret = vlc_stream_vaControl( p_sys->stream,
+                                      (i_query == DEMUX_SET_TITLE)
+                                          ? STREAM_SET_TITLE
+                                          : STREAM_SET_SEEKPOINT, args );
+        if( i_ret == VLC_SUCCESS )
+            ReadyQueuesPostSeek( p_demux );
+        return i_ret;
 
     case DEMUX_GET_META:
         return vlc_stream_vaControl( p_sys->stream, STREAM_GET_META, args );
